course: dictionary
lesson: 9076
title: Slop and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Slop can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to slop means to spill liquid over the edge of a container, often messily. «Mum told me not to slop my juice when I carried the tray.» The words carried the tray are the clue: careful carrying is about not spilling.
explain: As a noun, slop is watery, unpleasant food, or waste food and dirty water. Farmers sometimes give slops to pigs. Look at the words around the word: pigs and farm tell you which meaning fits.
explain: In Australia and New Zealand, «Slip, Slop, Slap» is a sun-safety rule. Here slop does not mean spill at all: it means put on sunscreen. «In Australia children learn to slip on a shirt, slop on sunscreen, slap on a hat, seek shade and slide on sunglasses.» The list of things to wear tells you what slop means.
fact: Slop can be a verb or a noun, so its meaning depends on how it is used in the sentence.
fact: «To slop» means to spill liquid over the edge of a container, often messily.
fact: «Slop» can mean watery, unpleasant food, or waste food and dirty water fed to pigs.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «Slip, Slop, Slap» means slip on a shirt, slop on sunscreen, slap on a hat.
fact: Children learn «slip, slop, slap, seek, slide» to stay safe in strong sun: a shirt, sunscreen, a hat, shade and sunglasses.
exercise: «In Australia children learn to slip on a shirt, slop on sunscreen, slap on a hat, seek shade and slide on sunglasses.» What does slop mean in this sentence? | Eat a bowl of soup | Spill a drink | Run very fast | *Put on sunscreen
exercise: In «slip, slop, slap, seek, slide», which item goes with slop? | sunglasses | a hat | a shirt | *sunscreen
exercise: The farmer carried a bucket of slops to the pigs. What are slops here? | Clean water for the garden | Sunscreen for the farmer | *Waste food and dirty water for pigs | A soup for dinner
test: Which meaning fits best in «The soup slopped over the edge of the bowl»? | Left in the fridge | Made a loud noise | *Spilled over the edge | Ate it all up
test: In «pig slops», what is a slop? | Bright sunshine | *Waste food and dirty water | A sun hat | Clean water
exam: Which statement about slop is true? | It is only a noun | It can only mean sunscreen | It means very old | *It can be a verb or a noun, with different meanings
